+
+#### [OCRmyPDF](https://github.com/OCRmyPDF/OCRmyPDF)
+> **Description:** OCRmyPDF adds an OCR text layer to scanned PDFs while preserving the original document, which makes it especially useful for legacy insurance files, broker-submitted scans, and back-office archives that are image-only. The README focuses on searchable PDF conversion, deskewing, cleanup, compression, and batch-friendly command-line operation. That is a strong fit for agencies that want a preprocessing layer before search, retention, or downstream extraction. GitHub shows the project as a mature Python repository with an MPL-2.0 license, a substantial community, and ongoing maintenance; stars are about 24k+, and the repo remains active in 2026.
+
