+> **Description:** docTR is a deep learning OCR library for document text detection and recognition. The README highlights fast pipelines, pretrained models, and document-oriented use cases instead of generic computer vision benchmarks. That makes it practical for extracting insured names, policy numbers, dates, and line-item text from forms and correspondence where layout quality varies. It is also a good option for teams that want to customize OCR in Python rather than rely on managed services. GitHub lists docTR as a Python project under Apache-2.0; stars are roughly 8k+, and visible repository activity continues in 2026.
