+> **Description:** PaddleOCR is an end-to-end OCR toolkit built for text detection, recognition, layout analysis, table extraction, and document parsing across many languages. For insurance agents, that matters when you need to pull data from declarations pages, applications, endorsements, inspection reports, and claim attachments without building an OCR stack from scratch. The project README emphasizes practical deployment, model variety, and document AI coverage rather than only raw OCR. GitHub metadata checked from the public repo shows an actively maintained Python project under Apache-2.0 with a large contributor base; stars are roughly 56k+, and public activity remains visible in 2026.
