+### Category Gap Note
+There is still a real gap in public GitHub repositories built specifically for insurance agents, insurance CRMs, comparative raters, AMS replacements, or carrier appetite search. Most open-source coverage today is in adjacent layers such as OCR, RAG, speech, and workflow automation. This list reflects that honestly instead of padding it with unrelated SaaS products.
+
+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for insurance agents in 2026?
+For most agencies, the strongest open-source stack starts with `PaddleOCR` or `OCRmyPDF` for intake, `Whisper` or `faster-whisper` for calls, `RAGFlow` or `Dify` for knowledge assistants, and `n8n` or `Activepieces` for orchestration. The best choice depends on whether your main bottleneck is document handling, call intelligence, or workflow automation.
+
+### Are there any AI tools built specifically for insurance agents on GitHub?
+Very few. Public GitHub coverage is still much stronger for horizontal building blocks than for insurance-native applications. That is why this repository focuses on tools that materially help insurance agents even if they were not originally marketed only to insurance teams.
+
+### Which GitHub AI repos are best for processing insurance PDFs and ACORD forms?
+`PaddleOCR`, `OCRmyPDF`, `docTR`, `Unstructured`, `Marker`, and `Layout Parser` are the most relevant starting points. In practice, agencies often combine two or three of them: one for OCR, one for structure extraction, and one for retrieval-ready chunking.
+
+### What is the best self-hosted AI assistant for an insurance agency knowledge base?
+`RAGFlow`, `Dify`, `Open WebUI`, `Flowise`, `Langflow`, and `LibreChat` are the strongest self-hosted options in this list. If citation quality matters most, start with `RAGFlow`. If usability and internal chat UX matter more, start with `Open WebUI` or `LibreChat`.
+
+### Which open source AI tools help insurance agents transcribe and summarize calls?
+`Whisper` and `faster-whisper` handle transcription, while `pyannote-audio` adds speaker separation and `SpeechBrain` expands into broader speech intelligence. `Vosk` is a good option when fully offline or lightweight deployment is more important than chasing the newest large-model benchmark.
+
+### Can an insurance brokerage build a private AI workflow without proprietary SaaS?
+Yes, but it usually means assembling a stack. A common pattern is OCR plus document ETL, then a RAG layer, then workflow automation, with a self-hosted chat UI on top. This repo was built specifically to support that GitHub-first approach.
